    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "1.1 What was the defect, as opposed to the symptom?",
      "prov:value": "**The tell that you are fixing a symptom:** the fix names a specific instance. `j6t3` and `xgd8` in a rule, `document-ingestion.html` in a selector, one\nfilename in a condition.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xgd8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "1.2 What else has this shape?",
      "prov:value": "> `vq8g` again. A twelve-bean sweep over the store found **ten** using list\n> items, **two** using bold enumerations — and one, `dhvf`, using subheadings\n> and being **over-counted ten for four options**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean dhvf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "1.2a A sweep must report its own coverage",
      "prov:value": "> Measured 2026-09-23, sweeping the health checks for more findings whose\n> action could not clear them.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "1.3 Is the fix at the right layer?",
      "prov:value": "> `tcq2`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The two axes, and they go wrong independently",
      "prov:value": "Most over-generalisation is one of these. `vfr8` was both at once."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Four tells, all cheap to check",
      "prov:value": "Recognising three forms is\n   right; adding their counts gave `dhvf` **14 options where it has 4**. `thux` keys on `parent`\n   rather than `type: epic`, because `type` is a label a bean sets about\n   *itself* while `parent` is a fact another bean asserts about it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The strongest outcome is when the adversary reverses you",
      "prov:value": "Twice\ntoday the measurement said the opposite of the reasoning."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What this deliberately does not do",
      "prov:value": "When narrowing the\ngeneralisation costs something real — `tcq2` found the corner magnifier under\nthe staging banner, where raising it defeats the banner and lowering it costs\nthe position — report the measurement and the two options rather than picking."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Provenance",
      "prov:value": "Written 2026-09-23 from five fixes in one session, at the owner's ask: *\"try to\ngeneralize pattern of a fix. adversarty skill, did you genrealize too much...\nare you picking up unindeneded things.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
